{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggp3Ekzwt3tJ6cQxTy9s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three bands fit an octahedral d² complex with Dq ≈ 1702 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 639 cm⁻¹. I got these from the `ts_fit_spectrum` tool, and the residuals are all under 0.4 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Assignment** (all from the ³T₁g(F) ground term):\n- 15 730 cm⁻¹ is ³T₁g(F) → ³T₂g.\n- 24 030 cm⁻¹ is ³T₁g(F) → ³T₁g(P).\n- 32 750 cm⁻¹ is ³T₁g(F) → ³A₂g.\n\n**Hand check of Dq.** The ³T₂g and ³A₂g levels sit at 2Dq and 12Dq above the unperturbed ³F level. The ground term is pushed down by the same amount in both transitions, so the difference ν₃ − ν₁ is exactly 10Dq. That gives 10Dq = 32 750 − 15 730 = 17 020 cm⁻¹, so Dq ≈ 1702 cm⁻¹, matching the fit.\n\n**Hand check of B.** Using the sum of the two ³T₁g roots, 15B − 6Dq, I get B ≈ 639 cm⁻¹. My hand cross-check of the ³T₁g(F)/³T₁g(P) mixing matrix did not close, so I am relying on the tool for B rather than on my hand calculation. It may be an error in my matrix, which I did not resolve.\n\n**C is not determined.** The tool carried C = 3801 cm⁻¹ through as a default assumption. The three spin-allowed bands of d² do not depend on C, so I am not reporting it as a result.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1702, \"B\": 639, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three spin-allowed d2 bands fit Dq and B with sub-cm^-1 residuals; C is not constrained by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2162,"cache_read_input_tokens":7985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2162,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":663,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bc377ce-f2a6-4202-8ee9-ee033becd5ae","uuid":"2b8c7a5c-e262-47cf-af50-737ba43253